abstract:
A cluster is a dense region separated from other dense regions by sparse ones. That single reinterpretation frees clustering from convex shapes, removes the need to specify k, and gives outliers a place to go — DBSCAN is the only algorithm so far that can say "this point belongs to nothing". We define core, border and noise points, formalise density-reachability, show how to pick eps from a k-distance plot, and cover the varying-density weakness that HDBSCAN exists to solve.}
